          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:10",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And the men of his city, even the elders and the nobles who were the inhabitants in his city, did as Jezebel had sent unto them, and as it was written in the letters which she had sent unto them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29
          },
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 132
          },
          {
            "start": 139,
            "end": 142
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:11",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "They proclaimed a fast, and set Naboth on high among the people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:12",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And there came in two men, children of Belial, and sat before him: and the men of Belial witnessed against him, even against Naboth, in the presence of the people, saying, Naboth did blaspheme God and the king. Then they carried him forth out of the city, and stoned him with stones, that he died.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 116
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:13",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Then they sent to Jezebel, saying, Naboth is stoned, and is dead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:14",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when Jezebel heard that Naboth was stoned, and was dead, that Jezebel said to Ahab, Arise, take possession of the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, which he refused to give thee for money: for Naboth is not alive, but dead.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 127,
            "text": "TG Selfishness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Selfishness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Selfishness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Selfishness",
                "entryId": "tg-selfishness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:15",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when Ahab heard that Naboth was dead, that Ahab rose up to go down to the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, to take possession of it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:16",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And the word of the Lord came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:17",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Arise, go down to meet Ahab king of Israel, which is in Samaria: behold, he is in the vineyard of Naboth, whither he is gone down to possess it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 52
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:18",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And thou shalt speak unto him, saying, Thus saith the Lord, Hast thou killed, and also taken possession? And thou shalt speak unto him, saying, Thus saith the Lord, In the place where dogs licked the blood of Naboth shall dogs lick thy blood, even thine.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:19",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ahab said to Elijah, Hast thou found me, O mine enemy? And he answered, I have found thee: because thou hast sold thyself to work evil in the sight of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 94
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:20",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I will bring evil upon thee, and will take away thy posterity, and will cut off from Ahab him that pisseth against the wall, and him that is shut up and left in Israel,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 9:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 9:8.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 9:8",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 8,
                        "end": 8
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:21",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And will make thine house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah, for the provocation wherewith thou hast provoked me to anger, and made Israel to sin.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 168,
            "end": 170
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:22",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And of Jezebel also spake the Lord, saying, The dogs shall eat Jezebel by the wall of Jezreel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 9:36."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 9:36.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 9:36",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 36,
                        "end": 36
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:23",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Him that dieth of Ahab in the city the dogs shall eat; and him that dieth in the field shall the fowls of the air eat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:24",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "But there was none like unto Ahab, which did sell himself to work wickedness in the sight of the Lord, whom Jezebel his wife stirred up.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 21:25",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And he did very abominably in following idols, according to all things as did the Amorites, whom the Lord cast out before the children of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 21:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
